{"id": "x0178", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The circumference of the Earth is about 40, 07 5 kilometers at the equator. That makes it roughly four ten thousand kilometers around when you measure from one side to the other through the middle. It ’s actually a bit shorter if you measure along the poles because the Earth isn’t perfectly round; it’s slightly squashed at the poles and bul ged at the equator. So, in short, the equatorial circumfer ence is just under forty thousand five hundred kilometers.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
