{"id": "x0258", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I practice Kyokushin karate because it teaches me discipline, self- control, and the importance of hard work. The physical challenges help me stay focused and build confidence, while the training pushes me to overcome fear and face difficult situations head-on. It's also a way for me to stay fit and healthy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0266", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Helicopters are limited by the amount of lift they can generate with their rotor blade. So, you know, when a helicopter is flying slowly, it has more time to push air down ward and create lift. But as it gets faster, there's less time for each ro tor blade to push air down ward before it moves on to the next part of its rotation, so it can't produce as much lift at high speed s. That' s why helicopters typically fly slower than airplanes, which use wings that generate lift in different ways.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
